                    <table class="contentpaneopen">
<tr>
		<td class="contentheading" width="100%">
					Programmer's Python Data -  Time Zones			</td>
				
		
					</tr>
</table>

<table class="contentpaneopen">
<tr>
	<td valign="top">
		<span class="small">
			Written by Mike James		</span>
		&nbsp;&nbsp;
	</td>
</tr>

<tr>
	<td valign="top" class="createdate">
		Tuesday, 24 February 2026	</td>
</tr>


<tr>
<td id="IprogrammerMainArticleTextBody" valign="top">
	
	<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="contenttoc">
	<tr>
		<th>Article Index</th>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td>
		<a href="/programming/195-python/18685-programmers-python-data-time-zones.html" class="toclink active">Programmer's Python Data -  Time Zones</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	
			<tr>
				<td>
				<a href="/programming/195-python/18685-programmers-python-data-time-zones.html?start=1" class="toclink">Converting Times</a>
				</td>
			</tr>
			</table><div class="pagenavcounter">Page 1 of 2</div><p class="chaptertitle-western">Dates and times are difficult and more so because of the use&nbsp; of time zones.&nbsp; Find out what lies behind this in this extract from <strong>Programmer's Python:&nbsp;Everything is Data</strong>.</p>

<p class="western"><h2 style="text-align: center;">Programmer's Python<br />Everything is Data</h2>
<h2><strong>Is now available as a print book: <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09ZGBHMG9" target="_blank">Amazon</a><br /></strong></h2>
<h4><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/1871962587/ref=as_li_ss_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1531216392&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=programmer's+python+mike+james&amp;linkCode=ll1&amp;tag=iprog-20&amp;linkId=db656223ac3f0d25e57b1c329226c93f" target="_blank"><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="/images/stories/Core/Pythonlang/pythondata360.jpg" alt="pythondata360" width="200" height="288" /></a>Contents</h4>
<ol>
<li>Python – A Lightning Tour</li>
<li>The Basic Data Type – Numbers<br />&nbsp;&nbsp; Extract: <a href="/programming/195-python/15400-programmers-python-data-bignum.html">Bignum</a><span style="color: #ff0000;"> <br /></span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Extract:&nbsp;<a href="/programming/195-python/19004-programmers-python-data-rational-and-decimal.html">Rational and Decimal</a>&nbsp;<span style="color: #ff0000;">***NEW!!!</span></li>
<li>Truthy &amp; Falsey</li>
